 "Rhode Island's governorship is open after Dan McKee lost the Democratic primary, and Helena Foulkes enters the general election as a clear favorite over Republican nominee Aaron Guckian. The state leans Democratic by about eight points, and recent surveys from UNH, Emerson, and Opinion Diagnostics show Foulkes leading by roughly 22 to 27 points, with Guckian stuck near 17 to 19 percent.\n\nThe race's main wrinkle is a crowded independent field. Ken Block is campaigning on a change message and cites polling suggesting Guckian acts as a spoiler, though Guckian says he is staying in. Guckian also drew negative coverage for skipping a debate to seek Trump's support. Markets and every major rater agree the Democratic side is heavily favored, with only the size of the margin in real doubt.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 18.1}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.997, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9964, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9941, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9953, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9924, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9959, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9963, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9875, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9875, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9966, "margin": 19.0}]}